            <ArticleTitle>[Intestinal intussusception in young adults: literature review].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>533-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0100-69912009000600014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although intussusception is the main cause of intestinal obstruction in the pediatric population, it is a rare condition in adults, and when it happens, the clinical characteristics differ a lot from the pediatric group. The purpose of this article is to report a case of a 16 years-old male that was seen at the Emergency Room of the University Hospital of São Paulo with an intestinal intussusception as the first clinical presentation of a Burkitt lymphoma. A literature review was carried out and relevant aspects of the case are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
